itions "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< P_s"},{"type":"text","text":" are the source incidences, hyperedge by hyperedge in index order and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"within one in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sourceIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"P_s + q"},{"type":"text","text":" is target incidence "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"type":"text","text":", in the same order. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per-incidence array is indexed by edge position. A view is a snapshot, so its own positions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only until its next mutation: the view of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", inserting"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one cell shifts every later incidence by one)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every index member reads the base’s rows, shifted where they hold hyperedges:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"successorIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"outHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plus n, and of ","type":"text"},{"code":"n + p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"targetIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"predecessorIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"inHyperedgeIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plus n, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"sourceIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Graph algorithms therefore run on the view without hashing a vertex. The view","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"does not offer ","type":"text"},{"code":"_withSuccessorIndexRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whose contract needs edge positions in row order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Costs are as for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceGraphView"},{"type":"text","text":": O(1) reads on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":", which stores its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incidences; on another base a hyperedge’s incidence numbers are a range, O(1), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binary-searches and selects by rank, O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" is computed from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberRank"},{"type":"text","text":", O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/directedincidencegraphview"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:11Hypergraphs26DirectedIncidenceGraphViewV","roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Hypergraphs\/DirectedIncidenceGraphView.swift#L41","fileName":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView.swift"},"symbolKind":"struct","title":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"Hypergraphs"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"abstract":[{"text":"A directed hypergraph’s incidence graph, r